# Training artifacts. These are large (runs_v2 is ~470 MB and grows during a
# run: checkpoints, wandb state, eval videos) and are already backed up to
# gs://vc2-2026-checkpoints/<run_name>/ by the trainers' --gcs-bucket sync.
runs_v2/
videos/

# MkDocs build output
/site/

# Agent worktrees (git worktree checkouts created by parallel agents; the work
# reaches the branch as commits, never as files under here).
.claude/worktrees/

# WS4: recorded play-server demos (the BC dataset; ship them to GCS, not git)
demos/
*.demo.npz

# WS4 going online: the 40 MB cloudflared binary scripts/play_online.sh fetches,
# and the server/tunnel logs of a play session.
.tools/
logs/

# Local wandb run state. Same class as runs_v2/: pure training artifact, and
# every byte of it also lives on wandb.ai. (The run-2026071*/ dirs already in
# git predate this and are left alone rather than churning a delete commit.)
# NOTE the glob: `run-2026080*/` was dated and only matched August 1st-9th, so
# every run from the 10th on was left untracked-but-visible. `run-2026*` covers
# the year.
wandb/run-2026*/
wandb/latest-run

# Scratch traces from the t2a contact/displacement probes.
trace_ep*.npy

# Per-epoch sweep checkpoints. The 2g/2h sweeps write policies_ep*.pt every 20
# iterations across 27 runs -- 232 MB, against 3 MB for the log.json files that
# hold the actual results. The logs are committed; these are reproducible from
# them plus the recorded args, and the earlier hand-picked policies.pt files
# stay tracked because gates load them.
runs/competevo_port/*/policies_ep*.pt

# D3 3e: the port's own training run. The .p checkpoints are ~76 MB each and
# the log is the thing worth keeping, so the models directory is ignored and
# the logs are not.
runs/t2a_port/*/models/

# Rendered clips. Derived artifacts: every one is reproducible from a committed
# policies.pt via `render_sweep.py` / `eval_soccer2v2.py`, and the set is 66 MB
# against ~2 MB for the logs that actually carry the results. The inputs are
# versioned; the renders are not.
runs/d2_sweep_clips/

# D3 M3 E0 rollout videos. 81 MB of mp4 across 53 clips, and every one of them
# is already in wandb under d3_e0_ant_seed{1,2,3}_media, which is where anyone
# would actually look at them. The PNG contact sheets ARE committed, because a
# still of the final bodies is what the doc points at. Sidecars are upload
# receipts and mean nothing after the fact.
runs/d3_e0_ant/renders/*.mp4
runs/d3_e0_ant/renders/*.mp4.json
runs/d3_e0_ant/renders/*.mp4.json.sent

# D3 M3 E3. Same class as E0's renders: the clips are large training artifacts
# and every one of them is already in its arm's wandb run, inline with that
# epoch's metrics. The post-hoc JSONs are NOT ignored -- they are what the
# write-up and any later artefact source, so a result never has to be read back
# out of a training log.
runs/d3_e3_adversarial/renders/*.mp4

# D3 M3 E3 live-policy captures. 157 MB each, copied out of the trainer's own
# transient video checkpoint so the design population can be probed at the live
# epoch (best.p is frozen at epochs 0-3 on these arms). Same class as any other
# checkpoint: the RESULT of probing them is tracked in census/pop_*_LIVE.json
# and census/population.csv; the weights are not.
runs/d3_e3_adversarial/census/live_ckpt/
